{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TKTw3K3mk595mQVdrsUGin","type":"tool_result","content":"## The .ard/ contract\n\n`.ard/<issue#>/` is the only place agents leave durable output, and every file in it has one owner role. Issue directories are numeric, so they never collide with the role directories under `.ard/` (see Configuration).\n\n```\n.ard/\n  <issue#>/\n    issue.md             # scanner: the ask, findings, fingerprints, links\n    plan.md              # triage roles except the lead: each owns one `##` section, replaced in place on a re-run; the worker follows it\n    triage-lead.md             # one audit log per stage and role that ran: <stage>-<role>.md\n    triage-architect.md\n    triage-engineer.md\n    worker-engineer.md         # worker: what changed, test results, open issues\n    review-security-review.md  # reviewer: findings, verdict, what must be fixed\n    logs/                # full, redacted output of every agent run on this issue\n      triage-lead-<ts>.log\n      worker-engineer-<ts>.log   # one per agent step; test logs stay on the host\n    costs/               # controller: one usage record per job, any outcome (the issue body shows them as a table)\n      <job-id>.json\n```\n\n**Who may write what.** Close-out checks every changed file under `.ard/<issue#>/` against the job's allowlist:\n\n| Stage and role | May change |\n| --- | --- |\n| every job | its own role file `<stage>-<role>.md` |\n| `triage:product-manager`, `architect`, `designer`, `documentation-planner`, `engineer` | plus its own `##` section of `plan.md` (`## Requirements`, `## Design`, `## UX`, `## Docs`, `## Implementation`) and nothing else in that file |\n| `triage:designer` | plus any file under `design/` (write or delete) |\n| `triage:lead` | its role file only |\n| a custom triage role | its role file only, unless `config.yaml` gives it `plan_section: <heading>` (see Configuration) |\n| `worker:*`, `review:*` | its role file only |\n## Configuration\n\nConfiguration is by convention: a role exists because its directory exists, and `.ard/config.yaml` holds only global settings and overrides. No prompt path is written anywhere; ard reads `.ard/<type>/\n\n**Shared roles.** `roles_repo: {repo: <owner>/<name>, ref: <ref>}` in `.ard/config.yaml` loads role directories from another repository, so several repositories can reuse one role set. It is pinned li\n\n```\n.ard/\n  protected_paths: [.github/, .ard/config.yaml, .ard/scanners/, .ard/triage/, .ard/workers/, .ard/reviewers/, \"**/CODEOWNERS\", CLAUDE.md, \"**/CLAUDE.md\", AGENTS.md, \"**/AGENTS.md\", .claude/, .mcp.json, \"**/.golangci.yml\", \"**/.golangci.yaml\", \"**/.golangci.toml\", \"**/.golangci.json\"]\n160:**One committer for main.** Close-outs never push. They hand a file set to the controller's committer, which keeps i\n224:**The lint scanner** (`scanners/lint`, a `sh` script, one `jq` program and a Dockerfile that builds golangci-lint v2\n254:**Starter planning roles.** `ard init` also ships four planning roles, each writing its own `plan.md` section (`conf\n389:- the diff touches no protected path; the list comes only from `merge.protected_paths`, with no floor in code (decid\n445:merge:                       # defaults written by `ard init`; the list is the only source (no floor in code)\n472:Scanners also take `route` (`pending`, `none` or `needs-human`). Anything unset takes its default: intake in `label`\n474:**`ard init` proposes the starter `.ard/` as a PR (decided, #27).** It builds `config.yaml` and the starter roles in\n487:- **Planted repo config does not steer agents.** A branch can carry CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, `.claude/` settings, hooks\n489:- **Role files are human-owned.** The diff guard and the committer's code lane reject any worker change under `.ard/","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8328e4e2-1211-4885-a6f6-74fec4bedb87","uuid":"4046772d-6685-47f5-8447-c26b499c0f01","timestamp":"2026-1